<title>USA: Wickes Lumber revolving credit extended.</title>
<headline>Wickes Lumber revolving credit extended.</headline>
<dateline>VERNON HILLS, Ill. 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wickes Lumber Co said Friday it completed an agreement extending its $130 million revolving credit facility to March 31, 2001, reducing the company's borrowing spreads and modifying certain financial covenants.</p>
<p>The restated credit agreement includes an immediate 75 basis point reduction in the borrowing spread to 225 basis points over LIBOR and 75 basis points over prime, as well as further borrowing spread reductions if certain performance levels are reached.</p>
<p>Wickes supplies building materials nationwide.</p>
<p>	  ((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
